Since I didn’t have a real backend, I used json-server to simulate one.
First, I created a db.json file that contained structured e-commerce data such as users, products, cart, orders, payments, and notifications. This file acted as my mock database.

npx json-server --watch db.json --port 3000

API	Endpoint
Users	http://localhost:3000/users
Products	http://localhost:3000/products
Cart	http://localhost:3000/cart
Orders	http://localhost:3000/orders
Returns	http://localhost:3000/returns
Reviews	http://localhost:3000/reviews
Notifications	http://localhost:3000/notifications
